    71	An old man in Denvash had cut that leaf from his pad a long while ago, and had rolled a ruler in it for a boy who was going where there were no instruments. It had lain in a bag on the wrong side of a river for a month and more. And in that time the boy had walked off the end of another person's brass for three days and come to a marsh, and had stood at a fence of iron with a line going through it. He had not written one word of that west. The old man could not have known that there was a line. He had only known the boy.
