   805	- **The debt is paid.** Three self-readings on three different days (the 102nd; the night of the 119th; before light on the 120th), then all of it told to Oryn at once, and she was read only with her leave. **"The still place"** — Cael's private log label since Books 5–6 — is now a LOCATED finding in him and has been said aloud: to Oryn first, and to the other four on the 121st. Shape and sensation only: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log." No theory, no source, nothing about before.
   806	- **Teague is neither read nor asked** and knows nothing of the mechanism. He forfeited the four-mark weir slip to come (it was never set or paid); the axe-head hold's fence (forty) passes to the five for the cold term ("Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / "Ours,"); "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew is unnamed, the older healer of no Path included.
   807	- **The fourth site:** not entered, not named, its effect on a Path UNKNOWN and untested. Lira stopped one pace above the iron; the cordon's bars mark the line; nobody crossed and no sigil was tried. No watch-post; no dating on the cordon; the silhouette is ambiguous. Four stakes have been seen in all, each alone at an edge.
   808	- **The sites and the line:** the Ring (the Fallow), the Stair, the Hall, and the fourth, taken as lying on one line "as near as this skin can show"; no compass bearing is claimed for the whole. Only two maker sentences exist outside protected text: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) and "a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." Karis's hypothesis is still unstated; her window ends on the pencil stopping.
   809	- **Sheets: fifty-two** (eleven Ring, twenty-nine Stair, twelve Hall). The survey kit is on the table at Lowmarch: the case in tarred canvas, a cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke and the bar and a bright turned point, never driven, and a mallet; the dead man's ledger, shut, is Karis's (Seln gave it to her). The case of Seln's is shut and untouched; nothing is decoded.
   810	- **The end, at Lowmarch:** first snow on the 129th; the last ferry on the 130th with two letters west (Hesk; Vell) and Ephram's deferred to the first boat of the thaw; ninety-six in hand; nine lines in Pike's book and no number against the season; eleventh on the cloth; the ferryman's rope still owed. The instruments read true in Cael's hand.
   811	- **Bodies:** Lira's left arm slung and holding nothing, her right ankle never mended; her order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"); Oryn's crossbow is with Lira with ONE bolt left. Brom's shoulder opened, was mended a second time and is BOUND, not mended a third ("It will not hold three times this season"). Cael's three old ribs took Compression again (ten days; quiet on the 129th).
   812	- **Oryn** went north from the fork on her own terms, three weeks late at the oxen ford; an old woman's knee at Thornwater is promised "after the thaw"; her letter is printed once. Her brown mule is with the crew; the mill's grey jenny is with Oryn (she left by the left road on it and reached Thornwater on it). [Corrected at close from the Sol recheck.]
   813	- **Owner defaults standing at book end:** #48 (season-blind; yards; six protected lines amended, listed in B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md), #49 (the protected "Path… mine" log wording, verbatim), #50 ("Six years I've wanted a face", verbatim), #51 ("Tomorrow makes three", verbatim).
   814	
   815	### Review record
   816	All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial, cold read, source-distance (**0 tracked passages**), plan / canon / protected-text audit (nineteen line fixes applied by the coordinator: the protected units restored, the final count corrected to twenty-seven, Teague's forfeited slip, the fourth site kept strictly outside, three extra maker or intent assertions removed, the kit itemised).
