   183	## 5. POV plan
   184	
   185	**Cael ≈87% (≈261,000 words).** It is close third, tinted by his habit of cataloguing. The source's long, accumulating "catalogue" sentence is his signature, and the edition keeps the habit while breaking the chains (§7.4).
   186	
   187	**Cutaways ≈13% (≈39,000), five characters at 2.3–3.0% each.** Each is brief: 1,200–2,500 words, placed as a scene inside a Cael chapter, never as an alternating-POV chapter.
   188	
   189	| Cutaway | Budget | Placement (guidance; the author owns it) | Allowed to know | Must NOT know or show |
   190	|---|---|---|---|---|
   191	| **Vastin** | ≈8,000 (4) | M2: the last miles to the Line and the ferry (the three people who told him "go to the plank"; the page in his coat). M4: the outer district's "first honest district". M6: alone after the leaf ("aimed"). M9: the court's rim at night. | His career; what he read; the citation; "no key"; the technician's line **and the bar**; the completion report; his knee; his own declining of the second reading. | **The date's arithmetic.** He never computes the deep-layer date against Cael's Kindling. The integration mechanism (he is never told). The directive and the objection before the 305th. The two seals' names. Any wish to *ask* to join, or any vote (Book 9). The Arbiter–apparatus connection (his sentence stays stopped even in his head). |
   192	| **Karis** | ≈7,500 (3) | M1: a winter night with the kit's index (her want; the cord reads wrong only for him, and she refuses a theory). M5: decipherment (board numerals; the first letters). M8: the night after the lamps finding (the refusal held in her own head). | The sheets; strata; the index (as unreadable until the 298th); the leaf (after the 293rd); the lamps finding. | The Rune finding (nobody knows it). The integration of Rune before Cael tells Lira. **Drawing the line**: her interior names that the sentence exists and refuses it. The deep-layer date as Cael's Kindling. The leaf's content before it is read aloud. |
   193	| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
   194	| **Oryn** | ≈7,000 (3) | M4: the north circuit (Oxhollow's gate; the wrist; a birth). M6: a hold child's Kindling witnessed from outside. M9: the night after the first death. | Her readings; the still place as "nothing, everything round it"; twelve then thirteen currents; the mechanism (her Tide was taken at her direction). | **The leaf** (she has not heard it). The Rune finding. Any patient dying under her hands before the pass. An explanation of "Same as you". No cutaway at the court itself. |
   195	| **Teague** | ≈7,000 (3) | M1: the upper inn in winter, watching the five; the young one asking to learn; the wrist. M7: deciding the contract's terms; the meadow. M8: the watch's hut after the Span, counting. | His crew; Force and its line; the contract; the board; that he does not read. | The integration mechanism, including any suspicion that the boy took his Force. **The young one's name.** Any reading or writing (he does not read). |
   196	
   197	**No cutaway may disclose a reserved truth (§11) or any sequence lock (§13).** A cutaway may show a person's private want and an independent decision. It must not reveal a fact the plot later "discovers" in Cael's POV.
