editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-243-The plate tipped. Cael saw only two things: a darkness as broad as a door rising at the plate's edge, and the two halves of it parting like the shells of a mussel. Then the stone was not there. The plate fell back with a slap that wetted the six of them to the knee, and the water rocked, and was clear.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-244-
