editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-262-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-263-"Fourteen."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-264-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-265-The plate there tipped, and dropped, and the rings spread out from it and died against the kerb.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-266-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:267:"It was eleven for a thing that lay where it fell," said Karis slowly. "It is fourteen for that."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-268-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-269-"It had farther to come," said Seln.
