editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-382-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-383-*Hundred and eighteenth day. The edge of the third one, at the track's end. A marsh, and the reeds stop where the sigils stop. One bar, thirty-three, old, and no second. A hall in the middle of it, and a thing under the hall's floor that a carter told the healer nobody has seen whole.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-384-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-385-*Seln wrote its rule in Karis's book with his own hand. He has never done that.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-386-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:387:*Anchor: one point, set on a plate at the kerb's foot, and held for sixty counts. The first that I ever set. It came at eleven and stayed with it till I let go, and while it did I had nothing else at all. Not counted in the number. I'll not call a trial a use.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-388-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-389-*Deployment since the Line: twenty-three.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-390-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-391-*In at first light. Karis hasn't said if since the Stair.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md-392-
