editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-46.md:59:"He's just told you what it is. It's got a ruled edge and a word for itself. I don't need it read to me a third time." Her right hand had closed on the knot. "There's a walk on that oak at fifty that nobody's scratched, a string of salt to the middle holds before the pass shuts. There's a fence at forty, the day the hold comes off it. That's ninety marks of work that was posted by people who want a fence. We'd be down from both before the snow."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-46.md-60-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-46.md-61-"And the circles?" said Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-46.md-62-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-46.md-63-"I'm coming to them. You said four wheres. One's walked. One's this, with a paper nailed across it." She nodded at the sheets on Seln's knee. "The third's a long way south and east, with no road inside a day of it, and nobody's put a price on it at all. So we go and pace that one, on our own time, with a healer at the edge. I'm not saying leave them alone. I'm saying I'll not walk into the one that somebody's paying us to walk into."
