editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:87:The book was another matter. It was a page and a half of distances, set down honestly by a man with a knotted cord, and a line that stopped. A person at the back of this file needed it every evening of her life; and she kept a box in which, by her own rule, nothing was written of anybody that he had not heard to his face.
