editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md-147-"Nor have I. Sixty yards, four-strand." He knocked a last cake of ice into the river. "I'll not want it this side of the thaw. There's one more crossing in her, tomorrow, if that shelf lets me; the post comes down to the far bank for it. Then I take my lines in."
