editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:11:"It's sitting where she laid it. You'll not undo that knot, and you'll not have anybody undo it who hasn't forty cold terms of knots behind her. When you're down, you go to that woman before you go to your supper."
