editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:185:Karis had her lamp lit by then. She had set a point on its wick with her own hand, outside that line, and she had the long cord laid along the feet of the bars with Cael at its far end. There was no call for anybody's foot. The line was marked at every pace in iron; no foot was needed to find it.
