editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:187:She laid it twenty times. At each cord's end she set her short cord from the last bar to the line that the long one would next take, as she had on three other rounds. Cael, holding the lamp for her, saw that the short measure did not come to the knot that it had always come to. It came to half.
