editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-144-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-145-He had been at it since the morning, as he went at anything: a thing at a time, from the beginning, leaving nothing out. He did not have an answer. But he could state the whole of the question, and he had learned at a healer's table that this was most of the way.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-146-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-147-"I want to read it out," he said. "The whole design. Stop me where I've got it wrong."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-148-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md:149:"There's a paper, priced so that we'd come. There's a floor at the end of it where a Wind can't run, and an Iron Skin is a big man, and an Ember can't light her own lamp, and a Shadow has a knife and fifteen years. There's a bolt, placed to bring a healer over a line. There's a fence behind her. There are four bows on a rim, far enough back that we can't reach them and near enough to shoot anybody who climbs. And there's a night." He drew a breath. "Every piece of it does one thing. It takes away what one of us can do. It's a list with six names on it and a line through each."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-150-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-151-"Five names," said Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-152-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-153-"No. That's the part I've been all day finding. It's got six. It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-154-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-160-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-161-"Then that's what I can't do. I can't shout. If one of them sees a thing work on this side of that stone, there's a boat." He went through them aloud, since four of the people in that room knew them as well as he did. "The Wind cracks. The heavy one would lay the grass flat for thirty feet. Fire's fire; the Pressure can be seen gathering; the edge rings. That's five that shout. The read and the Compression are no use past the length of my arm, and the tenth does nothing at all in a fight."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-162-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-163-"That's eight," said Brom. "You've ten."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-164-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md:165:"There's the one that I keep shut. It was made for not being seen. And there's the one that I had from the hand on the Ostrand road." He looked toward the place where the healer was. "I was inside a thing like that fence once, with nineteen points round me. I let it go from where it touched me, and the whole of it came down like a row of stitches. I've done that one time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-166-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-167-"Can you do it to this?" said Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-168-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md:169:"I don't know. I tried it a second time, on a doorway, with Lira on the far side, and I couldn't get hold. I could see it and I couldn't reach it; seeing isn't reach. I'd have to find where this one's made fast, and get my hand on that place, from the inside. I can't see any of it from farther than ten feet." He made himself finish. "And it's better than two hundred yards from here, with six of them looking down."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-170-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-171-The room took that in for the space of several breaths.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-172-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-50.md-173-"Then you go up alone," said Seln. "At dusk. With the one that you were given."
