editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-126-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:127:It was the cord that Cael's eye went along first, since it was the only thing there that was going anywhere. It ran out over the floor toward the eastern wall, pale and thin, with a knot in it at every fifth span, and it lay as straight as a ruled line for half the width of the room. There it stopped. The rest of its length lay beside it in a coil that nobody had paid out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-128-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-129-Somebody had been measuring from the middle of that room to its wall, and had got half way.
