editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:161:Cael thought of a man kneeling where she knelt, with that mallet in his fist, in a room under the ground. He had struck it once, and looked. He had struck it a second time, harder. And then he had laid the mallet down beside the bar, quite neatly, and had not struck a third.
