editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:179:It was a field ledger, bound in limp hide, no bigger than Hesk's, with a pencil lying in its gutter. The leaves were ruled in faint blue, with a narrow column at the left hand and a wide one beside it; and the wide one was written from top to bottom, down a page and a half, in a small upright hand that used the pencil hard.
