editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-191-"I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-192-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-193-He went on to the next line before anybody could ask him again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-194-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:195:"Then there are distances, measured in cords, as she measures; his cord is that one, knotted at the fives. He begins at the edge. *North station to floor.* *East station to floor.* There are eight of those, by the points of the compass and the half-points, and against every one of them he has put the same figure."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-196-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:197:"His stations are the old irons," said Karis, to the wall. "There was a bar at each of those eight points this morning, scaled as the old one at the stone is scaled. I had a turf within a boot of every one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-198-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-199-"Then this is the book of whoever drove them." Seln kept his eyes on the leaf. "I put five cold terms on the old iron at the stone, and I see no cause to alter that for his book."
