editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md-329-They were on the ridge at dusk, on that same day, half a mile short of where the road tips over, when he saw it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md-330-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:331:There was a light first. It was small, and low down, where the dark ground was; a point of fire that did not flicker as a brand flickers. Before he had fairly taken it in, there was a sound that he knew as well as his own name, since he had walked eleven cold terms beside a Wind, long ago, in another crew. That crack was a Wind's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md-332-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md-333-He put up his hand, and his three stopped behind him.
