editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-49.md-295-"The rest have held," she said, after a long look. "It's not gone through. It's opened where it was newest." She was already tearing a strip from the tail of Cael's shirt, which he had held out to her. "I can't shut that either. I can bind it, and I can tie it higher, and you can keep it against your chest until there's a sky over us."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-49.md-296-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-49.md-297-She bound it. She tied the sling again, shorter, so that the hand lay almost at the collar-bone.
