 succeeded in 0ms:
22:- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
25:- **Teague's crew** winters at Lowmarch: four plus the healer of no Path. His term: "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted."
38:- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say."). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
39:- **Teague** turns west with three practitioners and the healer of no Path. **The young one is dead**, buried under stone at the pass's east mouth. His name was said once by the broad man and is never written. Teague carries Cael's letter to Hesk. "Next spring. Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes."
51:1. **KEEP — The winter frame (S1, 131st–264th).** The ferry has gone and the count has stopped moving. Inventory: nineteen, ten fragments, 96 marks. The winter is priced: "Meadow rate is four a month for a crew that's on my sheet" / "Eleventh", twenty paid in front, leaving 76. Teague's chin-lift across the yard; the season line left blank on purpose.
52:2. **KEEP — Pike's winter board and the fence (140th).** Two days out to the axe-head hold. Forty-one posts. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. Forty is paid at the gate: 116. PAID becomes the tenth line.
56:6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her spring's first stops. Nobody asked her.
63:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (his Kindling day; five years and a hundred-some days; "six" is the office's rounding), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
78:28. **KEEP — The road east (295th–297th).** The bridge (five piers counted; the crown not looked at). The spring. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited** ("Here"): the stick briefly off the ground; "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted." The feeling of being *known* is entered. Lowmarch at dusk on the 297th. Pike: "Treswick. Survey read. Bearing." The season line is dated. Cael no longer reads pages the other way round. **Teague's term and contract:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that."; "The wall's still the wall."
83:33. **KEEP — The crest (303rd).** The watch-post: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, a two-timber barricade, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one winter." Teague: "Drawn?" "Nobody declares. Nobody dies … Noted?" / Teague's first **"Noted."**
