editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:23:- **The five at Lowmarch:** Lira (Wind, Iron R1 formal) has her left forearm slung and load-restricted by Oryn's order since the Ring, and the right ankle taped and unmended. She carries Oryn's crossbow. Brom (Iron Skin, Copper formal) has his right shoulder mended twice ("not three times this season"), then bound, and carries it still and forward. Karis (Ember, unranked by choice) holds 52 copied sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall), the kit's field ledger, the carter's map with four circles and the bearing, and the Ternhall straightedge. Seln (Shadow, Bronze) has the cache on his back, unopened. Cael has Hesk's brass straightedge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:27:- **The Compact:** it has reached across the Line twice, on paper (the completion report) and in person (the Stair's rim). It knows quiet ground exists and which crew walks out of it declaring. It does **not** know what works inside. The asset-restriction is pending. **Vastin is still inside**, writing nothing, with one window in Book 7.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:28:- **Who knows the integration mechanism:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn. Nobody else knows: not Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:32:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:34:- **Five sites lie on one bearing, ages ascending east.** The court is the fifth and the oldest, 1,012 m across, and the end of the line. It is **unnamed** ("the court", lowercase). The taxonomy is decoded: a stroke alone, a stroke and bar, a stroke and two bars.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:36:- **The crack:** a directive and a filed objection under two seals that Vastin could name and does not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:37:- **Vastin** is on the stick until day 30 of Oryn's month ("Thirty's the month"). He walks with the five **unadmitted**. He has not asked to join and nobody has asked him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:38:- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say."). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:41:- **Count at the rim:** "Six. Six and no mule." That is Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Vastin. The word is "West."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:42:- **Body ledger at close:** Brom's forearm is bound (bolt, pass) and he has a week of colours. Karis's left hand is bound and will scar ("It'll leave a line"). The broad man's leg is knit and his shoulder bound. Teague's arm faces a splint warning. Vastin is on day 29 of 30. Cael's ribs "will carry. They'll hurt."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:52:2. **KEEP — Pike's winter board and the fence (140th).** Two days out to the axe-head hold. Forty-one posts. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. Forty is paid at the gate: 116. PAID becomes the tenth line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:54:4. **KEEP — The anomaly (168th).** The yard paces forty-two strides for everyone and "forty-one and a piece" for Cael, three times. The Ternhall edge reads a hair short in his hand and Hesk's edge a hair long. Karis's ruler sentence is said twice: a rule, then not a rule. Logged: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:56:6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her spring's first stops. Nobody asked her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:58:8. **KEEP — The ferry (277th).** Vastin arrives alone, in a brown coat, with an ash stick, a pack mended with cord and a bad knee. "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." Pike prices him: "What'd he do?" → "Then he's nothing yet." He pays a copper and a half for bread. Teague reads his hands a step longer than a crew looks. Lira's face for men in grey doesn't fit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:59:9. **KEEP — The long table (277th midday).** The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, their first words ever. The short thing: resigned or walked. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence; Vastin's new fact is "Cannot. There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail dead-ends at Treswick. Vastin has nothing to do afterwards. "Why us." Oryn on the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that can cross the Line. Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only: "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks; Vastin's close (§10). The ferry goes west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:60:10. **KEEP — The handover (277th evening)**, in Vastin's stated order. First, the records: a courier's flat of six years of survey abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), six rows, "More than four", and the completion report as the last sheet. Second, the page: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". Third, the technician's sheet: the deep-layer line and the brush bar; Karis copies it and writes "not read". Seln goes still and does not say the sum. Vastin's vertigo; Karis owns the response. Cael's hand stays a hand's width from the page. Nobody says *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:61:11. **KEEP — The slip (278th).** Clearance at the cut below the shoulder hold, twenty. "Ours" twice. Pike writes a sixth line for the healer. Vastin is not on the sheet and walks at the back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:62:12. **KEEP — The cut (279th).** Iron Wall is first shown: a plane across the road, rooted, and therefore loud. Brom fights silent with a rock. Lira works the scree. Cael bursts away, then goes still on the scree; the pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap. Seln in the heap. Five dead and three into the sink. Costs: Brom's foot; **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson: "The wall held the line. And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." / "You do now." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:63:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (his Kindling day; five years and a hundred-some days; "six" is the office's rounding), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:65:15. **KEEP — The last day of the road (281st).** Lira makes the same discipline of the crown, unasked. The reading inward, a fourth and fifth time: "a cord on a stone"; the instrument is wrong for a stillness. Vastin sits; "You were the instrument. I was the error." Vastin's confession, narrowed (ruling 18): "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why." Cael gives him the instrument's nothing. It is not friendship; it is ground. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:66:16. **KEEP — Treswick's outer district (282nd).** The grey bridge is older than the walls. The outer gate counts and does not ask. The mule at the trough. The inn with two doors: 136. Each of the crew looks in their own way. "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once." "They shoe by the tier." The road to the registry crosses the square, and the promise holds. Seln's report: the quarry; the provision; hands by count, up to four; the clerk; the exposure. "Four hands." / "I've two." "Entered by count. That's the door." The close (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:68:18. **KEEP — The provision (284th).** Four hands go up by count: Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin. Seln is not on the count. The square is avoided by Seln's route. The clerk does not ask and writes "four". **Lira's ladder does not pull** ("Four hands." / "Four." / "Right."). The iron door. Cleon pulls the iron to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:70:20. **KEEP — The yard door (285th).** Vastin's reflex: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —". **Seln answers truthfully** (ruling 25; Gate 27): "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was." The narration enters that Seln did not lie. "I'm sorry." / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:71:21. **KEEP — The marks (285th–287th).** The lamp trade. Cleon's board is matched to the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit**, verbatim. "Same make." Cael wants it turned on himself and does not say so. **Brom's yard:** he rights a cart with his back, no Path, is offered the life, and picks up the box on the bound shoulder. "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." **Seln's night walk** from a roof below the walls: "I looked at it." Vastin: "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." Cleon's close (§10). The 288th–289th are undramatized in the source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:72:22. **KEEP — The alley (290th, dusk).** Six faceless attackers: four above with a crossbow, two below with staves, one of the four a signaller on the landing. Vastin roots the cut wall to wall ("there is no round"). Nobody declares. Brom with a rock, Lira's drop, Cael still at the plane's foot ("the reason"), Seln's weighted cord from the roof. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave; none taken, no faces. Costs: Karis's left hand (a step's edge), bound by Brom with thread and teeth because no healer inside the gate would touch it; Vastin spent, the knee again. **The Iron-Wall notice** (§10). "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered" / "It's entered." Not told. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:73:23. **KEEP — The reader (291st).** By the carts' street in daylight. Cleon's inside: "An instruction leans … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." **Acquisition at "there".** Cael tells Lira first ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then Cleon at the bell. "You did what." "That's not supposed to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water; **the warning**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael take the case up together. The notice on the stair. The eyes are paid on the last flight. "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:74:24. **KEEP — Dividers (292nd).** Hesk's parcel and note. The meal: four marks, two cups kept for Karis and Oryn, Seln's slip read and burned ("Closed"); 130 marks. Vastin and the cups: "Out here you count who's owed a seat." The first inventory written inside walls (§12 C10). **The station's light is "not steady" for a count of one**: a pressure, "an instrument turning toward him". It becomes the fourth entry on the page. He does not cross; the promise holds at its first cost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:75:25. **KEEP — The leaf (293rd morning).** It is read aloud **once** by Karis (§9). The chronicle leaf is **marked**. Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers: two pages. The copy with the gap drawn. "Older. Made. Us."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:76:26. **KEEP — The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. **Lira first:** "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom's price. Seln keeps the cache "a while longer". Karis's two pages, then she falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: imperfect → corrupt → "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, said aloud (§10). "I want to stand in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:78:28. **KEEP — The road east (295th–297th).** The bridge (five piers counted; the crown not looked at). The spring. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited** ("Here"): the stick briefly off the ground; "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted." The feeling of being *known* is entered. Lowmarch at dusk on the 297th. Pike: "Treswick. Survey read. Bearing." The season line is dated. Cael no longer reads pages the other way round. **Teague's term and contract:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that."; "The wall's still the wall."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:80:30. **KEEP — The grade cracked (298th morning).** Three marks. Cleon's list puts the mark at the kindling and the mark on a sheet in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point lies past the fourth, on the line. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:81:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:84:34. **KEEP — The Span (304th).** First exchange: the watch's declaration is unanswered; Brom takes bolts on Iron. Teague goes through the middle (the barricade a body's length back) → **Force acquired** at a stride. Recoil: wrist, then elbow. The watch reforms. **Width:** "Nothing was gained inside" is entered first. "By count": five over stake thirty-four (Cael, Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin), four on the shelf. They walk to the pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east, unpursued. The win sentence (§10). The broad man goes over the sink's edge in the fourth second; Teague does not turn. Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers' nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's bill. **The Span** at noon: an arch on two piers over the sink, carvings on the piers' inner faces, the bearing "Through". Nothing happens on the crown. The thirteenth listens. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:85:35. **KEEP — The shale camp (305th).** The blanket. The rows lean along the bearing. The point is fixed. **The lamps finding** (§10). Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Cael does not add his own third page (the Kindling date). **The directive and the objection**: "That's not a monolith. That's a crack." Seals unnamed. "The Compact … Yes. Part of it." The broad man's "Aye". The healers' third exchange (hands in the other's work). Seln on the pass. The fixed close (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:86:36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall woman's first words to the six in a year.** The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall woman reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:88:38. **KEEP — The court (307th).** It lies low, and the plain is worn down to it. 1,012 m across (159 cords). The stratum under everything. The first cut ("The others are copies"). The bearing ends, with no sixth. The council. **At the line:** every sigil dark at the same stride; the reactions: Lira's "Right."; Brom pricing the stump; Karis's "It's the first one."; Seln's count; Vastin's line (§10). Oryn steps in one stride: "Nothing. Everything, round it. Same as you." It is unanswered. Teague steps in one stride and steps back: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough … Field's mine. This isn't field." The turning begins. Lira's fixed exchange. "Wait here."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:90:40. **KEEP — The ledger, the letter, and the dawn (307th night–308th).** Teague goes west carrying the letter; Oryn goes north; "Six. Six and no mule."; Vastin is unadmitted; "West." The closing prose (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:110:| **NEW — The ferry's first landing** (277th, high water) | quiet landing | 1,500 | Rope and flood. Vastin is seen holding a physical line, with no Path, before anyone knows it is him. Iron Wall must not show before the cut. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:119:3. **Vastin learning the crew's doctrine and "to be nobody"** (≈5,000, distributed). Day one of the border road is a silent-movement drill: walk silent, signal by hand, nobody declares unless meant to be loud. Then the cut's lesson, the spring's "Draft nothing", the yard door's "Be nobody", his week of moving toward the lamp and stopping (four times, then two), and the first order he takes and keeps (Millrace).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:140:| **Lira** | To find out what she is without a ladder | Asks Oryn to mend the ankle (her first ask since Norhold). Fights on through the arm's first warning (M2), then listens at the second. Keeps her registry paper in her coat and goes up as a hand. Looks at the whole ladder and it does not pull. Holds her question at the court ("Well?") and accepts "on the road". | 12 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:141:| **Brom** | Worth without a number | Prices Vastin at three hundred miles. Takes the cart's weight on the good shoulder and pays for it. Declines the broker's post by picking up the box. Says "Good" to Cleon. Carries at Teague's leave. | 10 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:142:| **Karis** | To be right and believed, with a primary source | Learns the kit. Makes the case for west. Owns the response to Vastin's flat. Reads the leaf once and asks that nobody say it back. Keeps two pages at a spring, a hole and a fire. Sits with Vastin after the pass. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:143:| **Seln** | To keep his old life undecided and his own | Tells only Brom about the posts. Sets the sheet before Cael without a word. Teaches Vastin the first thing he ever teaches anyone. Truthful deflection at the yard door. Walks the tiers and decides nothing. Keeps the cache "a while longer". Climbs the swept scree. | 10 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:145:| **Vastin** | To dig one thing up before he's done; to learn to navigate without authority | Walks three hundred miles alone. Carries the case unasked. Consents to be counted as a hand. Holds the wall with nothing behind it. Asks for the wall to be entered. Does not name the seals. Takes Oryn's order. Does not ask to join. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:148:| **Pike** | An honest ledger | Prices the winter. Prices Vastin at nothing yet. Leaves the season line blank, then dates it. | 4 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:155:The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:159:Each person keeps their own comic habit. Brom says "It's a boot" and gives one-word essays ("They shoe by the tier"). Pike speaks ledger. Oryn: "Everybody says that now" and "I'm going to have to find another word". Lira finds an essay in a single word. "Noted" spreads through the cast like a borrowed tool, in the sequence locked in §13. Running jokes: the mule's empty chair; the mule as the only one of twelve who never knows what happened; the ferryman watching people use his river; Vastin's good manners from a man "served all his life and never once fed". When pain is in the room, humour stops performing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:168:| 2 | No Sanction | 7–12 | 30,000 | S2, S3 (+270th–276th) | Bring Vastin in through the board and hand over the three things in his order; the book's question arrives as paper. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:171:| 5 | No Authority | 27–33 | 35,000 | S10, S11, S12 | The archive's first days; Vastin unlearning his name; Cleon's bones; Brom offered the life; the alley and the eleventh. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:179:**Quiet-movement statement:** Movement 4 is the book's one deliberately partial-quiet movement. Its tension is legal and bodily: a [SHATTERED] body enters a Compact city whose top holds a station. Its learning encounter is the reading inward (the instrument fails). Its physical load is labour: four hands, three tiers, two gates, a bad knee and a box. It may carry one small physical beat of the author's choosing, but it does not need a fight. Every other movement has at least one fight, set piece or learning bout.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:191:| **Vastin** | ≈8,000 (4) | M2: the last miles to the Line and the ferry (the three people who told him "go to the plank"; the page in his coat). M4: the outer district's "first honest district". M6: alone after the leaf ("aimed"). M9: the court's rim at night. | His career; what he read; the citation; "no key"; the technician's line **and the bar**; the completion report; his knee; his own declining of the second reading. | **The date's arithmetic.** He never computes the deep-layer date against Cael's Kindling. The integration mechanism (he is never told). The directive and the objection before the 305th. The two seals' names. Any wish to *ask* to join, or any vote (Book 9). The Arbiter–apparatus connection (his sentence stays stopped even in his head). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:193:| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:194:| **Oryn** | ≈7,000 (3) | M4: the north circuit (Oxhollow's gate; the wrist; a birth). M6: a hold child's Kindling witnessed from outside. M9: the night after the first death. | Her readings; the still place as "nothing, everything round it"; twelve then thirteen currents; the mechanism (her Tide was taken at her direction). | **The leaf** (she has not heard it). The Rune finding. Any patient dying under her hands before the pass. An explanation of "Same as you". No cutaway at the court itself. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:216:| 277 | Ferry; Vastin; long table; handover |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:218:| 279 | The cut; **Vastin's knee (Oryn's month: day 1 = 280)**; 138 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:234:| 296 | Shoulder hold; the cut revisited (Vastin day 17) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:241:| 304 | The Span (Vastin day 25); fragment thirteen (123) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:242:| 305 | Shale camp; lamps finding; the crack (Vastin day 26) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:258:| **Iron Wall (Vastin's Path)** | Witnessed at the cut (M3) and the alley (M5) | Rooted; the man is the plane's foot; it cannot chase; it is loud to anything that hunts discharge; reserve spent to the floor; the knee | Shown three ways: road (punished), corridor (rewarded), slant (the pass) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:259:| **11 · Iron-Wall-adjacent** | Acquired in the alley's quiet middle minute (M5) | Notice verbatim (§10). Deployment none | **Entered, not told**; the debt to Vastin stands |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:277:- Tiers and Paths in Teague's crew, in Vastin, and in Treswick's machinery (Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver; passes; tier gates; the smith's two forges; the provision's columns).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:286:- **Supporting cast:** many small beats each (§3.D), 0.1–0.7 per 10k per person. No single deuteragonist takes the budget. Karis and Vastin run highest (≈14 each across the book); Pike and the young one run lowest.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:321:- **The cut (M3).** A hundred strides of road cut to a cart's width, with scree on both sides and a frozen runnel a stride wide down the middle. A sink lies fifty metres below on the north side, iced and in shadow; there are eight hounds. Positions: Brom on stone at the south edge with a rock; Vastin a stride behind him; Lira on the south scree; Seln on the north scree, unseen; Cael twenty strides west, past the sink; Karis, Oryn and the mule at the east end. The decisions: the wall goes up and everything turns to the loudest thing; Brom and Lira work its south end silently; Cael bursts **away**, then goes still on the scree as the lock beat lands; the pack returns to the wall and breaks on it; the heap; the runnel. The opponent learns too: the den has learned the road. Costs to carry: Brom's foot; Vastin's knee (a month); Cael's burst bill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:322:- **The alley (M5).** Twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no doors. There are four at the top (a crossbow and a signaller on the landing) and two coming up from the yard gate with staves. The plane sits at the second flight's top step, wall to wall; Cael stands two feet below it. Brom has a loose step-stone. Lira drops from the second flight. Seln's cord comes from the roof onto the signaller's arm and the rail. It lasts "a minute and some". The opponent's plan was built for a declaration and meets a wall and a rock. Costs: Karis's hand; Vastin past his limit; Brom's good shoulder used wrong.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:324:- **The pass (M9).** A dry defile a hundred strides long with a loose-stone stream-bed. The west wall is scree to a shelf two-thirds up, carrying two timber-braced stacks, one with a roped dead pine; the east wall is sheer. The wall is a lean-to slant, high edge at the west wall ahead, low edge at the mouth behind. There are seven numbered volleys: Brom's forearm (1); the wall up (2); the fall (4); the broad man (5); the young one (6); Seln over the lip (7). Cael's push takes the second stack along the shelf, not off it. Teague goes up the stair left-handed; the tall woman reverses her spear. The team breaks along the ridge. **Win sentence:** Seln removed the team's ability to hold the high ground by climbing the slope its own rig had swept clean, and the wall bought him the climb.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:336:- **Two pages, no line.** The leaf and the lamps finding are never joined: not in dialogue, not in any interior (including cutaways), not in the narration. Vastin's sentence stops twice (in the chamber; on the shale). The words *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* are never used for Arbiters.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:350:4. **Vastin's page (S3):** "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:353:7. **Directive and objection (S20):** "Findings under the fifth column to be held. Not for onward transmission. Not for citation. Not for the seat." / "Objection entered: the holding of a finding is not the finding's disproof. Refer to the seat." / Vastin: "Somebody wanted this buried. Somebody else put it in writing that it shouldn't be. That's not a monolith. That's a crack."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:358:12. **Fragment eleven (S12):** "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:365:18. **Vastin at the fire (S16):** "I believed it was imperfect." … "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*." … "At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." / Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I did." / "His?" / "No. I read it, after. I did not sign it." … "I would have." / "Yes," Lira said. "You would have."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:368:21. **The court (S23–24):** Vastin: "I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it." … "This is where they drew it." / Karis: "It's the first one." / Lira: "Right." / Oryn: "Nothing," … "Everything, round it." … "Same as you." / Teague: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough." … "Field's mine. This isn't field." / at the centre: "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:370:23. **Pike (S2; S17):** "What'd he do?" / "Nothing," Vastin said. "Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." And the 297th line: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:371:24. **Vastin's papers (S8):** "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once, so that nobody asks twice."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:383:- Vastin (B6): "I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:389:- **Ch1 closing log (270th):** "The ferry runs when the ice goes. Karis has a bearing, an index she can't read, and a language she can't read, and she says the answers are in a border archive nobody's opened since before the Compact. I've spent five years staying out of registries because a registry is where they file you. She wants me to walk into the oldest one on the continent. The kit reads everyone but me. So does the world, mostly. Nineteen. Ice goes next week. West, and inside, for the first time since the academy above Ostrand — which is a sentence I did not think I'd write again." And the 168th: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:391:- **S2 doorway:** "You came through the board," / "I came through the board." / "Then you already know it doesn't care who you were." / "I'm learning," Vastin said. **S2 close:** "Because a council would file it," Vastin said, "and I spent forty years being the man they sent to make sure the filing held. I know exactly how deep a thing has to be buried before no one goes looking. This is deeper than that." … "I helped bury smaller things. I'd like to dig one up before I'm done." Also: "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." / "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." / "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:392:- **S4 lesson and log:** "The wall held the line," … "And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." … "I have never once in forty years needed someone else to be the reason." / "You do now," / "I know fields. I don't know packs." … "I'll learn or I won't." Log: "Vastin fought. He rooted the road and nearly got eaten for it — a wall's no good if you're the only thing making noise behind it. He knows fields. He doesn't know packs. He'll learn or he won't. Watched an Iron Wall go up two feet from me. Filed it. Note the day: an Archmarshal took a wound out here and there was no one to report it to. He looked almost free. Almost."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:394:- **S6:** "I'm not an archive person." / "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second." / "You go inside, you don't go near the station. Not the steps, not the square. You promise me in that log of yours, because I've seen what the log does to you." / the log entry: "The fork. Oryn north; five holds; routing, not the other verb. Her term, given at the fire, taken in the log because that's the form she'll take it in: inside Treswick I do not go near the station. Not the steps. Not the square. Written here so she can read it, and so I can." / "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." / "Not the steps," … "Not the square."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:395:- **S7 log:** "Ran the reading on myself again. Same nothing at the center. I think the reading can't do it — you can't measure a stillness with a thing that only feels movement. I need an instrument for what doesn't move. Karis says there's a man in Treswick who reads how things are built. Maybe that's the instrument. Maybe I'm about to hand a stranger the one question I've never let anyone hold. Tomorrow. The walls are close enough now to have a color." ("color" stands in the log, per ruling 19.) Also: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." / "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:398:- **S10:** "Older than [UNBOUND]," / "I know that hand." / "Being believed — " … "It's the end of being able to be wrong." / "Give me a week." / "I'm sorry," / "Don't be sorry," Seln said. "Be nobody." Log: "Karis has been looking for this room her whole life. Cleon's been sitting in it for thirty years waiting for her. Vastin tried to open a door with his rank and nearly closed all of them — an Archmarshal's worth nothing here, which he's taking about as well as I took [SHATTERED]. Down here the stone's older than the Compact, so the Compact doesn't reach. First place inside walls I've ever stood where nobody can file me, and it's a hole under a city, and it's because everything down here is older than the machine that files. Karis says give her a week. I've got a box to carry and a promise to keep about a station upstairs. I can wait."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:400:- **S12:** "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered somewhere, since I'm not the one who keeps the ledger any more." / "It's entered," Log: "Eleventh. Iron Wall, from Vastin, in an alley, while he held a line for us with nothing behind him but the decision to. It's not Brom's — Brom gets harder, this holds. I've spent five years learning to give ground and disappear. Now I've got the opposite in me, from the man who spent forty years being the wall they put in front of people like me. He held it for us instead. I don't have a word for what that is. I wrote it down anyway."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:404:- **S19:** "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / "Noted," / "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times," / win sentence: "The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would." / Teague's arm: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that now," Log body: "Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth. Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend. The Span's the fourth site and the Compact fenced it, years ago by the scale on the iron, and left men on it. They knew. They've always known. The bearing runs through it and keeps going, oldest-last, and the oldest one's out there in the deep edge, quiet since they built the machine. One more site. I've wanted to stand in the middle of it since Karis said *someone made this.* Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:422:| Vastin's request and the 3–2 vote | 9 | Not staged, hinted or scheduled. He does not ask; nobody asks; nobody discusses whether he should. "Unadmitted." |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:436:- **C1 — Vastin's age.** The source states "Fifty-three, or near it" (S2), "at fifty-one" (S7) and "fifty-three-year-old" (S10). The universe ledger records 53. OWNER-DECISIONS #8/#17 default: *age never stated; career "forty years"*. **Edition: no stated age.** "Forty years" is kept as his own rounding (ruling 20). *Owner ruling welcome; it does not block.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:437:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** "five years" since the Kindling is correct and stays. Spans tied to the academy, the cache or Seln are anchored to events ("since the academy above Ostrand", "since a hearing", "since Norhold") rather than numbered. The single exception is Cael's own spoken rounding in the fixed S8 line, kept verbatim and heard as his rounding. *Owner may prefer to rewrite that line too.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:457:- **Lira asks nobody for anything** from Norhold until "Will you mend it." (266th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:459:- **Seln teaches nobody anything** before "Draft nothing. Just look." (280th, to Vastin).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:460:- **Seln and Vastin exchange no words** before the 277th long-table doorway.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:462:- **Teague's crew never drills under Vastin's wall** before the pass morning, when the doctrine is told to them once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:464:- **"Noted" adoption:** Vastin's first is the 298th (the grade); Teague's first is the 303rd (the crest); Oryn's "Everybody says that now" comes on the 304th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:465:- **Vastin** takes no order without walking it back before Millrace's "Stand there". He does not sit in front of the crew between the cut and the road's last post (281st).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:472:- **Vastin has not read the directive or objection** before the shale camp (305th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:474:- **The clerk** stays unnamed and "do not name" holds. He has not asked three things by the 291st.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:480:**Names pending owner approval: none required.** Every new figure the expansion needs is carried by role: the axe-head hold's factor, the carter at the ice road, the ferryman and his boy, Oryn's route patients (at Oxhollow and unnamed holds), the hold child at the Kindling, the broker's men, and the hood in the tail. This keeps the audio load low in a book whose cast is already heavy with role-names (Teague's crew must stay unnamed by canon). If the author finds a recurring role that needs a name in the audio, it is listed here for approval before drafting, and drafted under the proposed name per the edition's policy (RUN-LEDGER 18:41).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:482:**Existing names stay exactly as canon has them.** Never "Halcenvane" on the page; use "the academy above Ostrand". The registry collisions are untouched (OWNER-DECISIONS #6). **Audiobook read-through list** (carried): Cleon/Cael (KLEE-on/KAYL; never in one spoken run); Span/Stair; Treswick/Ternhall (keep them out of one spoken inventory); the O-onset stack Oryn/Oxhollow/Ostrand; Pike/Fiske. Places minted by canon only: Treswick, the Deepstacks, the Sunken Span, "the court" (description), the shoulder hold, the cut, the pass. **Do not name new holds** on Oryn's route. Use Oxhollow or Thornwater, or none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:488:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three holds and "Spring. Bring the map."; Teague's "Next spring" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael nineteen until his autumn birthday (about the 467th day), staged in Book 9. Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:19:"All eight. They've taken no harm from a stair or a wall, which is more than you deserved of them." She drew the wool up and tied her own knot, high, with the hand at the collar-bone. "It holds nothing. I said first snow, near enough, and I'll say when; you'll not say it for me because a flake's come down."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:127:Cael could not have said what. It was grey, and upright, and it was taller than a man; how much taller he had no means of telling, with nothing beside it to measure by and the better part of half a mile of dusk between. It was not a ring of stones. It was not a floor with a hole in it, or four walls. It had a top that was not level. That was all that the light would give him, and when he tried to hold more of it, the dusk kept the rest.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:161:He could have gone over. He knew only that he had crossed three such lines before and that the fragments had answered there; nobody had tested this line, and nobody would. He kept his boots beside theirs. It was a crew's line or it was nobody's, and he had learned on a white floor what it cost to hold a different ruling from the people whom he was ruling for.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:187:She laid it twenty times. At each cord's end she set her short cord from the last bar to the line that the long one would next take, as she had on three other rounds. Cael, holding the lamp for her, saw that the short measure did not come to the knot that it had always come to. It came to half.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:11:The six on the rim were where they had been all day: two on the brow above him, two away to the south, one north, and one far off across the low ground against the last of the light. The two on the brow were on their feet; the one with the bow had it up across his chest, spanned, and the other was holding his own hands out before him and looking into them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:81:He saw the fingers want to. He saw them hold their stillness for one breath, and for a second, with the heat coming up into them. Then they closed, slowly, and the hands drew back, and went down to the man's sides.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:123:"There. Back," she said. It came out of her on one breath, hoarse, as a person speaks who has been holding it since the morning. She opened her eyes and looked at her own left hand in the lamplight, back and palm. "The clock started again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:127:"Down. Here, on the blanket, on your left side. You, bring that light and hold it where I point. You, the pannier, the one that's on the grey." She had Brom on the turf before any of them had moved. "And somebody give me a knife that'll cut ash."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:129:It was Seln's. She had him kneel behind Brom's shoulder and cut through the shaft below the iron head, a notch at a time, while she held the wood still in both her fists so that it should not turn. It took as long as it takes to say a line over twice; then the head came away, and she threw it on the grass, and put one hand flat on the front of the shoulder and took hold of the feathered end with the other.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:149:"It held a stair. It's not going to hold anything else this season."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:151:"It did hold it," said Lira. Her voice was small. "I'd have gone down the other twenty on my head."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:173:"A fence that failed at dusk, at its knot, which was set on an iron bar that stands upon the very edge of the place; and directly afterward a boy, who stood up out of the old road beside that bar and declared." Seln folded his hands. "Nobody on that rim saw anything between the stair and the bar. I asked Lira what she saw from the thirty-fourth step, and she says that she saw a stair. They will write that he crept up a rut in bad light while they were watching a hole, and that a knot tied a hand's breadth from such an edge is a knot which nobody should have trusted. A man who lays fences for his living would far sooner put that on paper than the other thing, and he has no cause to think of the other thing at all. It holds."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:199:*Shadow: once, from the fourth step to the old bar. Lira saw it go, from below. Seln turned his back. Three were round the door. The six were two hundred and sixty yards off, with a lip between; not one had a line to me. Let go in the rut. It holds. Dead to the elbows; I had to watch my own hand.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:81:On the second morning the road swung away south toward a hold whose smoke they could see, and the brass did not go with it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:219:They walked. Though not one of them could have said so yet, that was the rule of the place, and it kept them company the whole of the way in: a hundred and eighty-five yards, which Karis counted under her breath, with something in the reeds holding its station on them for exactly as long as they did not stop.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:367:"If it comes for one of you, I've a fragment that it will go to first. I held Anchor for sixty. I don't know that I can hold it for longer." He looked at Seln. "There's nobody on any rim. If the floor opens, I'll use what I have."
