editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/B7-RECONCILIATION-H-RERUN.md:364:   **Replace with:** `It is later on the hundred and thirty-first morning, at Lowmarch's lower inn hearth, after Oryn's letter and Karis's "Someone made this pattern." The first snow fell on day 129. The last ferry crossed and its lines were taken in on day 130; the ferryman is not taking ropes in now. A hand's depth of snow lies on the road. There are five at the lower inn. Lira's left arm is slung high and holds nothing; her right ankle is taped and unmended; she has Oryn's crossbow, hook and one bolt. Brom's shoulder is mended twice and held in four yards of webbing. Karis, Ember Iron Rank Three, has 52 sheets, the dead man's ledger, the four-circle map and Ternhall brass. Seln has his locked case, shut. Cael is nineteen, with ten fragments, 27 deployments behind him, and a still place untouched by order. Hesk's brass is in his coat. The living purse is 96 marks; the sealed reserve is separate. The brown mule is with the five. Teague's five are at the upper inn.`
