editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:25:- **The fence at the axe-head hold** (~140th, ~3,000 for the set piece). This is two days out on the winter road. A shale-back herd shelters on the fence line's slope and must be moved without stampeding, with no Path that matters. Lira is benched in her sling and reads the herd for them. Brom reads the line of posts like a wall. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. The factor pays forty at the gate and asks no name: 116, and the tenth line, PAID.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:27:- **The silent yard** (two or three bouts across the winter, ~1,500 each). Teague's crew and the five spar in the frozen meadow with steel and bodies, and no Paths. Cael loses to the tall woman's spear reach, then makes a visible correction. She never says a word to any of the five. Lira coaches from the bench, one-armed. The rival clock appears on the page. Teague is the better field captain.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:30:- **Karis's case grows in pieces** through the winter. She says the full sentence about west on the 263rd. The thaw comes, and the Thornwater road opens on the 264th.
