+# Book 8 plan — Book 7 reconciliation audit, §H final re-run
+
+**Audit seat:** Sol, independent continuity audit  
+**Date:** 2026-10-11  
+**Authority used:** the CLOSED Monroe 1.3 Book 7 manuscript, chapters 45–60; Book 7 `STATE_LEDGER.md` AFTER MOVEMENT 6, 7 and 8; the Movement 8 audit and recheck; coordinator overrides O3–O6; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md`; and the complete Book 8 map, entry ledger and nine packets.  
+**Scope:** final amendment instructions only. No Book 8 plan file has been changed by this audit.
+
+## Verdict
+
+Book 7 now closes on the **hundred and thirty-first morning**, at the lower inn hearth in Lowmarch, after the carter brings Oryn's letter through a hand's depth of snow. The first snow fell on day 129; the last ferry crossed and its lines were taken in on day 130. Book 8's day-131 opening therefore stands and its relative day spine does **not** shift, but its opening must be placed after the Book 7 hearth scene, not while the ferryman is still taking in the ropes (`chapter-59.md:3,47–49,121–147`; `chapter-60.md:47–95,219–265`).
+
+All former **PENDING B7 M7–M8** facts are now determinable. The old forecast is substantially right on day, fragment count, cash, sheets and Pike's line count, but it is wrong or incomplete on the Oryn debt, Karis's rank and knowledge, mechanism-knower count, exact fourth-site radius, the ferry instant, the object/account inventory, capability rules and use counts, and several current quotations. Movement 1 is releasable **after** the ordered amendments below are applied and Book 7 is locked. Owner items #52–#55 do not block Movement 1; their deadlines are M3, M4 and M9.
+
+## 1. §H re-run — final answers
+
+| Re-verify | CLOSED fact and evidence | Final action |
