# STATE LEDGER — Book 8: Before the Paths (Monroe 1.3 edition)

This is the book's entry state, taken from canon (the Book 7 close in `universe/STATE_LEDGER.md`, Book 7 Ch23–24, and the source edition's Ch1 inventory). After each movement is drafted, append one section built from the surviving prose, not from the plan. Where the prose and the plan differ, record the prose and note the difference. The binding end state is `BOOK_MAP.md` §1. The sequence locks are §13, and the owner-facing conflicts are §12. If the edition's own Book 7 rewrite moves any seam fact below, reconcile this section before Movement 1 is compiled.

---

## ENTRY — Movement 1, chapter 1 (Lowmarch; the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line; first snow, the day after the ferry's last run)

### Bodies

| Who | State |
|---|---|
| Cael | Nineteen (turned nineteen in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **No birthday this book.** Ribs quiet since the marsh, healed under a healer's two days that became four. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. The ten fragments are at rest. The still place is untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". |
| Lira | Wind Path, Iron R1 formal (registry paper, carried unshown). **Left forearm slung and load-restricted by Oryn's order** since the Ring (bitten on the 96th; reopened at the Stair; mended twice). **Right ankle taped and unmended**, turned out a little from walking on it. She will not say the word *ankle*. She carries Oryn's crossbow. |
| Brom | Iron Skin Path, Copper formal. **Right shoulder:** bolt at the Stair, mended, reopened at the Hall, mended a second time ("Twice. It will not hold three times this season"), then bound by the healer of no Path. He carries it still and slightly forward, and it is unread by Oryn. Feet sound. |
| Karis | Ember Path, unranked by choice. Fit. Her voice, lost at the Ring, came back in Book 7. |
| Seln | Shadow Path, Bronze. Fit. The cache is on his back, carried and unopened. |
| Oryn | Tide Path, Iron R4 (provisional). At **Thornwater**, on her route. "Six, by letter." |
| Teague's crew | Wintering at Lowmarch's upper inn: Teague (Force; Bronze by a registry he stopped reporting to; about forty; a wrist that clicks), the tall woman (spear), the broad man (crossbow; a limp), the young one, and the older woman with the cloth bag (a healer of no Path). **All but Teague stay unnamed.** |
| Vastin | Inside the Compact, writing nothing (one window in Book 7). **Age not stated in this edition** (OWNER #17). "Forty years" is his own rounding. |
| Pike | Lowmarch's board-keeper. One arm. Keeps the board's room at the lower inn and has "chosen the smoke over the cold". |
| Hesk | At his shop in Denvash. His straightedge reached Cael on the last ferry. |

### Knowledge

**Cael knows:**
- His ten fragments, their costs and deployment notes.
- The still place: read three times; "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues."
- Four sites lie on one bearing. The Ring, Stair and Hall were entered. The fourth was paced from outside: 400 m radius, numbered registry iron a pace apart, at least forty stakes counted, not entered.
- His Path works inside the quiet ground. Every other Arbiter in the party fails at the same stride.
- The Compact surveys quiet ground, from the kit's ledger: a radius line, an index of forty-one kinds, the stroke-and-bar mark, and "third site confirmed on bearing".
- The faceless faction has reached twice, on paper (a completion report naming the crew that walks out) and in person on the Stair's rim. Asset-restriction is pending.
- Book 6's sentence from Vastin: "I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be."
- Karis's sub-layer: "under every station on the continent", since Ostrand.
- "Someone made this pattern" was asked once and is unanswered.

**He does not know:** that the index is a grade; the Architect; Treswick's archive or Cleon; anything Vastin carries; that instruments will read wrong in his hands. The last is discovered on the 168th.

**Who knows the integration mechanism:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn (Tide was taken at her direction). **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon.

**Karis knows:** the 52 sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall); that the carvings *command* rather than describe (from their shape, at the Hall); the strata; [UNBOUND] as a stratum limit (Book 7 Ch15, used once); the sub-layer; that the kit's index is an index, not what it indexes. She has read of the old scholars' provision in a register "years ago".

**Seln knows:** the faction's craft; that the completion report went west; the rival clock.

**The Compact knows:** that quiet ground exists, what it does to Arbiters, and which crew walks out of it declaring. **Not** what works inside.

### Resources

- **Cash:** 96 marks in hand. The inn's six for the back room is already out of the 102. Nothing owed.
- **Pike's sheet:** nine completed lines under the five names. The Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. **Eleventh** on the wall; Teague's four are top. The season line is blank, left so on purpose. The axe-head hold's fence slip (forty, HOLD, the five names) is taken, unpaid until it is done.
- **The kit** (Compact, registry-stamped, recovered at the Stair): the case; the pacing cord, knotted at the fives (twenty strides to a cord, end-loops worn shiny); stake number thirty-two (point bright); the mallet; the field ledger (the surveyor's square hand; the radius line; the one designation entry for the Stair, in an unreadable index; "third site confirmed on bearing"). No pen.
- **Karis's archive:** the 52 sheets in oilcloth; the carter's map with four circles and the bearing in pencil running off the edge; the Ternhall straightedge.
- **Cael:** Hesk's brass folding straightedge ("true to a hair"), Hesk's satchel and the log.
- **The mule.** Three boxes. The inn's back room for the sheets, paid.
- **Letters:** sent west on the last ferry to Hesk ("there's a roof") and to Vell (Pike's ledger; "The session still stands"). Received: Hesk's straightedge note; Oryn's letter.

### Fragments and progression (ten confirmed; the still place uncounted)

| # | Fragment | Source | Standing notes at entry |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Wind-adjacent | Lira | The burst; a locked landing beat after it; loud to anything that hunts discharge |
| 2 | Pressure-adjacent | "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (Feryn; audio rule) | A narrow, deep channel |
| 3 | Iron-adjacent | Brom | The bed; the surface read of load is the edge workhorse |
| 4 | Compression-adjacent | Reydan | Contact absorption; the frame that took the wyrm's strike |
| 5 | Ember-adjacent | Karis | Small, hot, exact; not used out here |
| 6 | Shadow-adjacent | Seln | Idle cost from waking; **seal held past the Line**; used unseen on the Stair's rim; never attributable |
| 7 | Storm-adjacent | Daeva | The suite; wide; asleep |
| 8 | Anchor-adjacent | unnamed hand | "Hold"; used both ways in Book 7 |
| 9 | Blade-adjacent | Ephram | Sharp, short |
| 10 | Tide-adjacent | Oryn | Partial; Iron; self and contact; engagement field *clinical*; **ask first, every time**; the reader cannot read the reader |
| — | The still place | — | Everything goes round it; untouched by order |

**Invent no numeric ceilings.** Costs are qualitative unless canon states a number.

### Relationships

| With | State at entry |
|---|---|
| Lira | Always first. Has read the log. Has a thing about the tops of walls since the training hall at sixteen. "What am I becoming if nobody's measuring" is still open. Has asked nobody for anything since Norhold. |
| Brom | Silent anchor; prices things; "It's a boot". Has found his worth in Pike's ledger, not a family's tier. |
| Karis | Holds a bearing, an index and a language she cannot read. Her rule: "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." |
| Seln | Says a thing once. Watches the rival clock. Gave the kit's ledger to Karis on the road and did not ask for it back. |
| Oryn | Terms of service; a route she owns. Owes Cael a reading "when you're not broken". Her rule is in her hand and his. |
| Teague | Rival captain; honest; priced. A term set in the snow. Better field captain, and the ledger says so. |
| Pike | The ledger's conscience. Stopped numbering the five because his book was "wrong about a crew by being too small". |
| Vastin | Off the page. The last contact was a borrowed office in Ostrand and one sentence. |
| Hesk, Vell | Letters. Hesk's next parcel (the dividers) arrives in Treswick on the 292nd. |

### Open threads at entry

- The fourth site: entered in Movement 8 as the Sunken Span.
- The kit's index: decoded on the 298th as a grade.
- "Someone made this pattern": answered in part by the leaf (Movement 6).
- The still place: deepened, not resolved.
- Oryn's reading of Cael, owed: the deep reading at Millrace (Movement 7).
- Lira's arm and ankle: released and mended at Thornwater (Movement 1).
- Brom's shoulder: read at Millrace.
- Teague's spring term.
- The faceless faction: three reaches this book.
- Asset-restriction pending.
- Carried and untouched: Reydan's "find me later"; Daeva's rematch; Vell's session; Hesk's full history; Coss's grade; the market stranger; the Iron Skin watcher; the Anchor operative's "account"; Brom's advancement review. Each gets a log line at most.

