+> - **Objects/accounts:** the tarred-canvas kit case, strap, cord knotted at the fives, unused stake 32 with stroke/bar and bright turned point, and mallet are at the back-room table; the dead man's ledger is shut beside them. Three boxes stand at the warm wall. The cart-and-gelding reserve remains sealed under five thumbprints in the third box, separate from the 96-mark living purse. The Fallow hundred and Stair 300 remain in Pike's box, unmarked and not crew-payable debts. The ferryman is owed 60 yards of four-strand rope, not wanted before the thaw. The forty-mark axe-head fence is taken and not begun. The six-mark back room is paid through the cold term.
+> - **Letters/animals:** Hesk's brass and note and Oryn's bark have arrived. Letters to Hesk and Vell went west on the last ferry; Ephram's is deferred to the first boat of the thaw. The brown mule is with the five. Oryn has the grey jenny and the thirty-foot three-strand rope.
+> - **Oryn:** last located at Thornwater, with route work north next. The old debt ran Cael→Oryn and is **PAID**: three self-readings and the full telling. Her withheld answer was never a debt. Her exact letter is: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` Lira's arm waits on Oryn's in-person word.
+> - **Teague's crew:** stays through the cold term at Lowmarch's upper inn: four practitioners plus the older healer of no Path, all unnamed except Teague. His exact term is: `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` He has the cold road; the five have the axe-head fence.
+> - **The Quieting:** four sites lie on one straight edge of the map. The Ring, Stair and Hall were entered. The fourth was seen and paced from outside at **440 yards and two strides** radius, behind registry-iron stake 34 repeated one per pace. It is unentered, unnamed, undated and untested; its grey central upright is unresolved and its effect unknown. `Someone made this pattern.` was said once and not answered.
+> - **Pike/the Compact:** Pike has nine completed lines under the five names; the ninth is the Stair and reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The first-snow season line is written with no number against it. The five names remain **eleventh**. The Compact has a Fallow completion report, the Stair rim's observations and a clerk's packet saying the crew kept the kit; it does not know that fragments work inside.
+> - **Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon. All six know the still-place phenomenon; only Cael and Oryn are shown hearing/saying its label. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know the fourth-site survey; Oryn, Teague and Pike do not know that result at entry.
