+| Snow/ferry sequence | The five reach Lowmarch in first snow on day 129; the ferryman says one crossing remains (`chapter-59.md:121–147`). The last ferry crosses at noon on day 130 with two fingers of snow, returns empty, and its lines are taken in (`chapter-60.md:47–95`). Oryn's letter arrives on day 131 through a hand's depth of snow (`chapter-60.md:219–231`). | Put this three-day sequence in the entry ledger and M1 packet. |
